!! A measured path stopped answering
   13:50:24 to 13:51:45  (1m21s)   rule reachability-lost, confidence 90%
   affected: 10.99.0.11

   1  13:50:24.303  l2.arp_binding_changed  10.99.0.11
      This is the last thing that changed before the path stopped
      answering.
      |  which caused
   2  13:50:35.545  metric.anomaly  10.99.0.11
      Probes to this address began going unanswered. Packet loss
      announces itself to nobody; it has to be measured, and it was.
      |  and then, without a known link
   3  13:51:45.463  metric.anomaly  10.99.0.11
      It later answered again, which bounds how long the outage lasted.

   root cause: l2.arp_binding_changed on 10.99.0.11 (confidence 90%)
   next:
      This is measured, not reported: the recorder sent probes and they
      did not come back. If the change named above was intended, the
      loss is a side effect nobody planned. If there is no change above
      it, the fault is beyond what this recorder can see from where it
      sits.

